From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: forward-declare airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available()

9999-15 (report unsupported PPE flow stats) added a call to
airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available() in airoha_ppe_flow_dump() before the
static definition of the helper, breaking the build with an implicit
declaration whenever CONFIG_DEBUG_FS compiles airoha_ppe_debugfs.c.
Forward-declare the helper. Upstream CI did not hit this because no
tested config compiled the file before.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@
 #include "airoha_regs.h"
 #include "airoha_eth.h"
 
+static bool airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available(struct airoha_ppe *ppe);
+
 static void airoha_debugfs_ppe_print_tuple(struct seq_file *m,
 					   void *src_addr, void *dest_addr,
 					   u16 *src_port, u16 *dest_port,
